  "text": {
    "action": "a right-handed baseball batter hitting the ball at the moment of bat-ball contact",
    "core": "Hips and shoulders turned square to the pitcher; front (left) leg straight and firm; back knee bent, back foot pivoted up on its toes; trunk tilted so the back shoulder is lower than the front; both hands together on the handle, right hand on top; rear elbow tucked close to the ribs; bat nearly perpendicular to the pitch line with the barrel about 30 degrees below the hands, sweet spot meeting the ball in front of the plate at about knee-to-thigh height.",
    "gaze": "Head down and still, eyes on the ball at contact.",
